# workflow

1) took a look in raw_data and controlled terminologies ( THIS ACTS AS INPUT LAYER) 
2) now transform the raw_data using mapping like  
SYS_BP → SYSBP  
DIA_BP → DIABP  
TEMP → TEMP  
PULSE → PULSE... \
( THIS ACTS AS PLANNER) 
3) Converted wide format to long format i.e one row is converted to multiple rows-one per test 
4) i generated new SDTM variable i.e \
STUDYID, USUBJID  
VSTESTCD  
VSORRES, VSORRESU  
VSSTRESC, VSSTRESU  
VSPOS, VSLOC
5) Generated a R.script so that there is no need of manually tranformation everytime. 
6) Then executed R.script via python
7) it produced a output file i.e vs.csv -----> THIS IS FINAL SDTM DATASET
8) i have validated the output that are there required columns, CT values, structure, and compared it with golden dataset.

# Why this Should be done and how it is used?

This project is needed to convert messy clinical trial data into a standardized format (SDTM) required by regulators like the FDA. 

generally hospitals collect the raw data from the patients but it may be messy, contain missing values, no standard names etc..\
so by this agent we can standardize the raw data according to the agencies \
we are simply automating the process instead of manual work.



